  {"type":"culture","title":"Η κρίση στη γλώσσα και στον Τύπο","text":"For a decade Greek public talk ran on crisis words: **η τρόικα** (EU, ECB, IMF), **τα μνημόνια**, **μνημονιακοί vs αντιμνημονιακοί** (the main political cleavage 2010–2015), **το κούρεμα** (the 2012 haircut on bonds), the 2015 referendum's **ΟΧΙ** later turned into a third memorandum, and **τα capital controls** (*κεφαλαιακοί έλεγχοι*), with queues at ATMs. The Aganaktismenoi in **πλατεία Συντάγματος** split into the 'upper square' (nationalist, anti-parliament) and 'lower square' (left, assemblies), a split that foreshadowed both SYRIZA's rise and Golden Dawn's.\n\nKnow your newspapers: **Η Καθημερινή** (centre-right, establishment), **Το Βήμα** and **ΤΑ ΝΕΑ** (centre / centre-left, same group), **Η Εφημερίδα των Συντακτών** (left, a cooperative founded by journalists of the bankrupt *Ελευθεροτυπία* in 2012), **Ριζοσπάστης** (KKE). The second column's phrases *αστικό κράτος* and *εργατικές – λαϊκές οικογένειες* are classic Communist-left vocabulary; spotting such markers tells a Greek reader the writer's camp within a sentence."}
